        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Nate Albert, Rod Stewart, Whitney Houston, Elton John, Def Leppard\n- Companies: Capitol Records, Universal Music Group\n- Roles: music executive, songwriter, producer, guitar player, Executive Vice President of A&R, rock singer\n- Organizations: The Mighty Mighty Bosstones\n- Albums: Back to the World\n- Radio Stations: WWBZ\n- Events: WWBZ format change\n\nFacts:\n- Rod Stewart was born on 10 January 1945 and is a British rock singer and songwriter.\n- Nate Albert was born in 1970 and is an American music executive, songwriter, producer, and guitar player.\n- Nate Albert was formerly a member of The Mighty Mighty Bosstones.\n- Nate Albert produced the album Back to the World by Street Dogs.\n- Nate Albert is the Executive Vice President of A&R at Capitol Records, which is a division of Universal Music Group.\n- On March 29, WWBZ replaced music by Whitney Houston, Rod Stewart, and Elton John with 24 hours of \"Rock Rock ('til you drop)\" by Def Leppard.",
